invariant: INV-7
file: quic_step.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: the Finished step derives the 1-RTT keys under the original
  version's labels, so a client that switched to version 2 protects its
  1-RTT packets under version 1's keys and the server, which derived
  version 2's, opens none. test/quic_loop_version.h switches a version 1
  client to version 2 against a server started in version 2 and requires
  a 1-RTT packet each way to open.

--- old
    uint32_t version = q->t.quic_negotiated_version;
    QUIC_KEYS_INIT_SUITE(&q->app_tx, version, q->t.wr_secret, q->t.suite);
--- new
    uint32_t version = q->t.cfg.quic_original_version;
    QUIC_KEYS_INIT_SUITE(&q->app_tx, version, q->t.wr_secret, q->t.suite);
